  "family_size": 51,
  "family": "One joint family: 44 CNN-reference contrasts, four within-decoder token-versus-feature contrasts, and three other-minus-proposed tokenization-gap contrasts.",
  "method": "Single-step exact synchronized participant sign-flip max-|t| test.",
  "statistic": "Per-contrast mean paired difference divided by its sample SD / sqrt(9). Recompute after each sign pattern.",
  "randomization": "Enumerate all 512 sign vectors. Flip each participant row synchronously across all 51 contrasts. Include identity and complete reversal; inclusive tails with floating-point tolerance. Do not center observed differences before flipping.",
  "adjustment": "For each sign vector retain the largest absolute t across all 51 contrasts. Adjusted p for each contrast is the proportion of these joint maxima at least as large as its observed absolute t. No extra Holm correction.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Participants are independent analysis units; three seeds are averaged within each participant.",
    "For finite-sample strong familywise error control, each participant true-null contrast vector is jointly centrally symmetric around zero under independent whole-row sign reversals. Marginal symmetry alone is insufficient.",
    "For pointwise location confidence intervals, participant differences are independent and symmetric about a common effect (equal to the mean when it exists).",
    "These distributional assumptions cannot be established from nine participants. Inference is exploratory and conditional on the studied data/protocol and shared frozen representation."
  ],
  "effect_direction": "Alternative minus reference error (mm); for CNN comparisons negative favors the alternative. All four representation contrasts use tokens minus encoder features; positive favors features. Gap contrasts subtract the proposed signed token-minus-feature gap from each other decoder gap; positive favors proposed.",
  "alpha": 0.05,
  "intervals": "95% pointwise exact sign-flip location intervals obtained by inversion of the univariate two-sided test. Not simultaneous; not used to assign significance stars.",
  "sensitivity": "Report all nine leave-one-participant-out mean differences and their range. Retain the previous global Holm results as sensitivity output; no method selection by result count.",
  "no_pseudoreplication": "Do not count 27 seeds or test frames as independent participants.",
  "minimum_possible_adjusted_p": 0.00390625,
